Django Wholesaler–Retailer ERP — Complete Project Knowledge
1. What is this project?

This project is a B2B Wholesale–Retailer Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) system.

Its purpose is to digitally manage the business relationship between:

                 WHOLESALER
                     │
        ┌────────────┼────────────┐
        │            │            │
     Products      Orders       Invoices
        │            │            │
      Stock       Payments      Ledger
        │            │            │
        └────────────┼────────────┘
                     │
                  RETAILER
                     │
             ┌───────┼────────┐
             │       │        │
          Stock    Customers  Sales
             │       │        │
          Orders   Invoices  Payments

Instead of managing everything through:

Excel
WhatsApp
paper bills
manual stock registers
manual payment calculations
separate customer records

the ERP provides one centralized system.

2. Real-world business scenario

Imagine a wholesaler named:

ABC Pharma Wholesale

and a retailer:

Sayam Medical Store

The wholesaler has:

Product:
Hing

SKU:
HING0001

Stock:
500 units

Selling Price:
₹190

MRP:
₹220

The retailer wants:

220 units

The retailer places an order.

The system checks:

Requested quantity = 220
Available quantity = 500

Therefore:

500 - 220 = 280

Wholesaler stock becomes:

280

Retailer's stock becomes:

220

The system then generates:

Order
   ↓
Invoice
   ↓
Payment
   ↓
Ledger

If the retailer pays only ₹10,000:

Invoice = ₹41,800
Paid    = ₹10,000
------------------
Due     = ₹31,800

The ledger records the outstanding amount.

This is the core business flow of the application.

3. Who uses the system?

There are primarily two business roles.

3.1 Wholesaler

A wholesaler can:

register
maintain business profile
connect with retailers
create products
manage stock
monitor low stock
monitor expiry
receive retailer orders
accept/reject orders
fulfill waiting orders
generate invoices
receive payments
maintain retailer ledger
track outstanding credit
manage shipments
view reports
eventually expose APIs
4. Retailer

A retailer can:

register
maintain shop profile
connect with wholesalers
browse wholesalers
browse products
view available stock
place orders
view order history
receive stock from wholesalers
maintain own stock
manage customers
create customer invoices
receive customer payments
track customer outstanding amounts
track shipments
view business reports

This is important:

The retailer is not only a buyer.

The retailer becomes a small business management user inside the same ERP.

5. Complete architecture

At a high level:

                     Browser
