PHASE 31 — Professional Git Workflow

Your GitHub repository should not look like:

final
final2
final-final
latest-final
new-final

Instead:

main
│
├── feature/payment-management
├── feature/customer-management
├── feature/shipping
└── fix/invoice-overpayment

Typical workflow:

git switch -c feature/customer-management

# coding

git status
git add .
git commit -m "feat: add customer management"

git push -u origin feature/customer-management

Then:

Pull Request
      ↓
Code Review
      ↓
Tests
      ↓
Merge
